!!! HTTP header fields.
!!!
!!! An array of pairs, not a map. Three reasons, and the first is decisive:
!!! an Ny generic map cannot be indexed or measured from a Matrix page, so a
!!! map here would push every header read into Ny. The second is that header
!!! order is observable — Set-Cookie must keep its order and its repeats, and
!!! a map either loses them or grows a second shape to carry them. The third
!!! is that a request carries a dozen fields, and a linear scan over a dozen
!!! pairs is not the thing to optimise.
!!!
!!! Field names are compared case-insensitively, as RFC 9110 requires, and
!!! kept in the spelling the sender used.

book nilweb.http.headers

read nil.std.core
read nil.std.text
read everything from nilweb.text.scan


public header-field begin record
    field name as text
    field content as text
end record


!!! --- An empty header set.

public no-headers returns array of header-field begin paragraph
    variable empty as array of header-field is []
    give empty
end paragraph


!!! --- The first value for a name, or "" when the name is absent.
!!!
!!! "" is also a legal field value, so a caller that must tell "absent" from
!!! "present and empty" asks has-field — the same distinction a map would
!!! force on every lookup, here only where it matters.

public field-value receives fields as array of header-field, name as text returns text begin paragraph
    repeat for each field-held in fields
        when same-folded with left being field-held.name, right being name then
            give field-held.content
        end when
    end repeat
    give ""
end paragraph


public has-field receives fields as array of header-field, name as text returns boolean begin paragraph
    repeat for each field-held in fields
        when same-folded with left being field-held.name, right being name then
            give true
        end when
    end repeat
    give false
end paragraph


!!! --- Every value for a name, in the order they arrived.
!!! Set-Cookie is the field that needs this; so does a repeated Via or Warning.

public field-values receives fields as array of header-field, name as text returns array of text begin paragraph
    variable found as array of text is []
    repeat for each field-held in fields
        when same-folded with left being field-held.name, right being name then
            append field-held.content to found
        end when
    end repeat
    give found
end paragraph


!!! --- Add a field, keeping any field of the same name that is already there.
!!! This is the one to use for Set-Cookie.

public add-field receives fields as array of header-field, name as text, content as text
    returns array of header-field begin paragraph
    variable out as array of header-field is []
    repeat for each field-held in fields
        append field-held to out
    end repeat
    append build header-field with name being name, content being content to out
    give out
end paragraph


!!! --- Add a field, replacing every existing field of that name.
!!! This is the one to use for Content-Type, Content-Length and the rest.

public set-field receives fields as array of header-field, name as text, content as text
    returns array of header-field begin paragraph
    variable out as array of header-field is []
    repeat for each field-held in fields
        when not (same-folded with left being field-held.name, right being name) then
            append field-held to out
        end when
    end repeat
    append build header-field with name being name, content being content to out
    give out
end paragraph


!!! --- Drop every field of a name. Removing an absent name is not an error.

public remove-field receives fields as array of header-field, name as text
    returns array of header-field begin paragraph
    variable out as array of header-field is []
    repeat for each field-held in fields
        when not (same-folded with left being field-held.name, right being name) then
            append field-held to out
        end when
    end repeat
    give out
end paragraph


!!! --- Parse one header line: "Name: value", with the value trimmed.
!!!
!!! A line with no colon is not a header, and gives back a field with an empty
!!! name — the caller checks for that and answers 400 rather than inventing a
!!! field called the whole line.

public parse-field receives line as text returns header-field begin paragraph
    value cut is nil.std.text::index_of with s being line, needle being ":"
    when cut is less than 1 then
        give build header-field with name being "", content being ""
    end when
    value raw-name is nil.std.text::substring with s being line, start being 0, length being cut
    value after is cut plus 1
    value remaining is (nil.std.text::length with s being line) minus after
    value raw-value is nil.std.text::substring with s being line, start being after, length being remaining
    give build header-field with
        name being (nil.std.text::trim with s being raw-name),
        content being (nil.std.text::trim with s being raw-value)
end paragraph


!!! --- The fields as they go on the wire, each line ending CRLF.
!!! The blank line that ends the header section is the caller's to write,
!!! because only the caller knows whether a body follows.

public render-fields receives fields as array of header-field returns text begin paragraph
    variable out as text is ""
    repeat for each field-held in fields
        set out to out plus field-held.name plus ": " plus field-held.content plus (crlf with nothing)
    end repeat
    give out
end paragraph


!!! --- The line ending every HTTP message uses.
!!!
!!! Matrix predefines `newline`, `quote` and `tab`, and no carriage return —
!!! there are no escapes in a text literal, so CR cannot be written as one. It
!!! comes from the character converter instead. A bare LF between header lines
!!! is a response some proxies and caches reject outright, so this is not a
!!! detail to leave to the caller.

public carriage-return returns text begin paragraph
    give nil.std.core::Convert.i32_to_char with code being 13
end paragraph


public crlf returns text begin paragraph
    give (carriage-return with nothing) plus newline
end paragraph
